{
  "id": "freecad_cw_part_045",
  "app": "freecad",
  "task": "Create one Part Design body. Create a circular base disk centered on the global Z axis with radius 26 mm and height 5 mm, spanning Z = 0 to 5. Create one raised cylindrical boss on the top face with radius 3 mm and height 6 mm, axis along global Z, centered at (16, 0) and spanning Z = 5 to 11. Make the disk an additive cylinder (FreeCAD's default name 'Cylinder') and the boss a Pad (default name 'Pad') of a circle sketch (default name 'Sketch'). Use Part Design Polar Pattern around the global Z axis through the origin to create 8 total boss occurrences evenly spaced through 360 degrees, so the boss centers lie on a 16 mm radius circle at 45 degree intervals. Save the completed model to /home/user/Unnamed.FCStd.",
  "env": {
    "files": []
  },
